# Product shape

Ctrl UI is an opinionated React + TypeScript design-system kit.

It is not a headless library. It is not a copy-paste catalog. React Aria is an implementation dependency for later composite layers, not the product.

First target consumer is an unnamed reference product and hoped-for pilot (B2B trip-booking), not a team that already installs the unpublished kit, not a committed adoption, and not a brand whose palette is copied into Ctrl UI. Do not name the employer or product in this repository. They would pick a kit like this because the live app mixes two kits (including a Material UI layer with bolted-on a11y), looks inconsistent, and a third Atomic Design iteration is desired — plus white-label theming without forking.

The kit MUST work in ordinary React. RSC hosts MUST be able to import it without a Next-specific package. Published modules that use client APIs MUST be marked `"use client"`.

A feature consumer MUST be able to install the public (or workspace) package and apply semantic tokens without cloning this repository.

The public package name is `ctrlds`. Workspace directory is `packages/ctrl-ui`. U1–U2 ship as a workspace package. npm publish waits until the first atom batch.

This foundation increment is toolchain + tokens. A consumer-shaped screen is out of validation until a consuming app exists.
